-- Animatica control layer for animatica-hero - generated by pipeline/dcc/max_build.py
-- from pipeline/dcc/max_controls_template.ms; edit the template, not this file.
--
-- The published .max carries plain bones (Euler_XYZ) + Skin, which is what the
-- Animatica plugin keys. This script puts an animator's control layer on top
-- and takes it off again without a trace:
--
--   fileIn "animatica-hero_controls.ms"
--   AnimaticaControls.build()      -- ctrl:* bones, CTRL_* controls, HI IK
--   AnimaticaControls.bake (interval 0 100)  -- key the bones (Euler_XYZ), then remove()
--   AnimaticaControls.remove()     -- back to plain Euler_XYZ, controls deleted
--
-- selfTest() builds, moves an IK goal, bakes and removes: it keys the bones, so
-- run it on a throwaway scene only (the pipeline runs it on an unsaved copy).
--
-- The controls are Maya's (control_plan.plan(): the same names, shapes, colours
-- and parents), each named CTRL_<Maya name>. A control that leads a ctrl: bone
-- whose parent bone is the one its Maya parent leads is spliced in between the
-- two; otherwise (hips_ctrl, spine_01: both under body_ctrl in Maya, while
-- ctrl:Spine1 is a child of ctrl:Hips) the ctrl: bone follows it through a
-- Position_Constraint + Orientation_Constraint (`constrained`).
--
-- Limbs (Maya's ik_/fk_ chains + blend): each limb segment (3 bones, + the toe
-- on a leg) has hidden fk:* and ik:* copies under the limb's parent ctrl: bone.
-- The FK controls are spliced into the fk: chain (CTRL_upper_arm_fk_L >
-- fk:LeftArm > CTRL_forearm_fk_L > ...); HI IK runs on the ik: chain (goal
-- hand_ik / foot_ik, swivel target a hidden CTRL_IK_<chain>_swivel led by the
-- pole, toe_ik spliced above ik:<toe>).
-- Each ctrl: limb bone has an Orientation_Constraint on its ik: and fk: copy,
-- weights wired to the limb settings control's ikfk (fk = ikfk, ik = 1 - ikfk).
--
-- Switches (custom attributes, MAXScript node properties):
--   $CTRL_arm_settings_L.ikfk        0 = IK, 1 = FK (also leg_settings_{S})
--   $CTRL_root_ctrl.hideInactive     1 = hide the limb's inactive FK/IK controls
--   $CTRL_root_ctrl.controlRig       0 = the deform bones play their own keys
--                                    (Euler_XYZ / Position_XYZ layer), 1 = rig

